`--verification-cache-solver-digest SHA256` (repeatable, or `verification-cache-solver-digest = [...]` in `dfyconfig.toml`) declares an audited solver binary by its SHA-256 digest, so that `--verification-cache` also replays results for it, for example for a reproducible source build of Z3 5.1.0 whose bytes differ from the release binary. The built-in list of audited Z3 release binaries is unchanged, and nothing else is trusted unless named. The solver binary is still hashed at run time: a binary whose digest is neither built in nor declared is not cached, with a warning when digests were declared, and the digest stays part of every cache key, so results from different binaries never mix. See https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/574.
